{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of Conjecture 380 of E. DeLaViña's \"Written on the Wall II\" (a conjecture of Graffiti.pc, 18 Feb 2009, status O): for every tree T on n > 2 vertices, γ_t(T) ≥ |D_even(T)| / (ecc(C) − 1), where γ_t is the total domination number, C the centre, ecc(C) the eccentricity of the set C (WOWII definition 52: the largest distance from a vertex outside C to C) and D_even the set of vertices of even degree. The proof establishes the stronger bound γ_t·(ecc(C) − 1) ≥ number of non-leaves whenever ecc(C) ≥ 2 (for ecc(C) ≤ 1, i.e. stars and double stars, the right-hand side is 0 or negative). It combines a double-counting bound 2γ_t ≥ (number of non-leaves) + 2 for a leaf-free minimum total dominating set (the Chellali–Haynes bound) with a short distance argument for ecc(C) = 2.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Ari Gilchrist"
    }
